  "edit": [
    {
      "sha256": "9c7cb35ae1b263581d9f20814fc3407a2368536f7c25b31d81896806ae135933",
      "descriptions": [
        {
          "path": [
            "description"
          ],
          "present": true,
          "source": "Change files inside your task root. For one or a few changes call this hand directly. For many mechanical changes a Python script is welcome: import praxis_hands as h and call h.edit, the same editor and shared write lock. Bare open().write or str.replace followed by writing bypasses both. Read first with inspect(action=read) and pass its sha256 as expected_sha256. replace: old must occur exactly once; all=true replaces every non-overlapping occurrence and reports the count. Overlapping matches still refuse; widen old. A confirmed after_sha256 is valid for the next edit. batch: files=[{path, expected_sha256, edits:[{old,new}]}]; every file is checked before any write. mode=snapshot (default) matches the original text; mode=sequential applies replacements in order. A batch stops at its first write failure; later files are untouched. No automatic rollback: reread and revert explicitly with fresh versions. write: new file or full rewrite. patch: unified diff, checked with git apply --check first. Reply is edit: JSON with status. confirmed: written and read back. refused: nothing written. in_doubt: writing may have happened; reread, never retry blind. partial (batch): some files written, some refused; inspect files. ok (patch or remote edit): backend reports success, no local readback promise. Host and Windows tasks refuse batch before sending it; use replace per file.",
          "key": "worker.schema.edit_tool.tool"
        },
        {
          "path": [
            "input_schema",
            "properties",
            "action",
            "description"
